course: dictionary
lesson: 12561
title: The word diagram
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A diagram is a simple drawing that uses lines, shapes and labels to show how something works, what its parts are, or how things are connected. «Label the diagram» means write the names on the parts of your drawing.
explain: You will meet diagrams in every subject. In science you might see a labelled diagram of a plant, in maths a Venn diagram, and in geography a diagram of a volcano. Look at the clues around the word: if the text talks about drawing lines, shapes and labels, it is a diagram.
explain: Diagram can also be a verb, but it is less common, and you will mostly see it as a noun. When you are unsure, ask yourself: is this a simple drawing with labels that explains something? If yes, it is a diagram.
fact: A diagram is a simple drawing with lines, shapes and labels.
fact: A diagram can show how something works, what its parts are, or how things are connected.
fact: A Venn diagram uses overlapping circles to show what groups have in common.
fact: «Label the diagram» is a common task instruction: write the names on the parts.
fact: Diagram is mainly a noun, with the plural diagrams. As a verb, to diagram means to show something as a diagram, and it is less common.
exercise: «The science book had a diagram of a flower on page ten.» What is a diagram? | *A simple drawing with lines, shapes and labels | A loud sound made by a machine | A type of sweet | A long story about a journey
exercise: In maths, which diagram uses two overlapping circles to sort things into groups? | Bar graph of the weather | Number line | *Venn diagram | Tree diagram
exercise: «Label the diagram of the volcano.» What does label mean here? | Fold the paper into a box | *Write the names on the parts | Cut out the picture | Colour the whole picture in
test: «Sam drew a diagram to show how water moves from the sea to the clouds and back.» What is the diagram showing? | A map of the school playground | A list of his favourite foods | *How water moves around, shown with lines, shapes and labels | A story about a boat trip
test: Which of these is the best way to show how the parts of a plant are connected? | A song about rain | A list of plant names with no pictures | *A labelled diagram of the plant | A poem about flowers
exam: «Maya drew a diagram to plan her science fair project.» What does this tell you? | *A simple drawing with lines, shapes and labels that explains her plan | A written story about the fair | A piece of music for the fair | A sound recording of her voice
